    "problems": "Validation accuracy is reported rather than training and test errors together, so the generalization gap cannot be computed. The Oxford_Flowers102 setup uses the dataset's test data for training and measures validation on the remainder. Accuracy results are averaged across at least three independent runs; no intervals beyond reported ± values are specified.",
    "rows_left_out": "No reported result rows were left out. Figure-only gradient-norm curves and loss landscapes are not included because they do not provide a numeric train-test gap or a listed-version measure.",
